{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1446","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Catching Cheaters"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given two strings $$$A$$$ and $$$B$$$ representing essays of two students who are suspected cheaters. For any two strings $$$C$$$, $$$D$$$ we define their similarity score $$$S(C,D)$$$ as $$$4\\cdot LCS(C,D) - |C| - |D|$$$, where $$$LCS(C,D)$$$ denotes the length of the Longest Common "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Subsequence"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of strings $$$C$$$ and $$$D$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You believe that only some part of the essays could have been copied, therefore you're interested in their "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"substrings"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Calculate the maximal similarity score over all pairs of substrings. More formally, output maximal $$$S(C, D)$$$ over all pairs $$$(C, D)$$$, where $$$C$$$ is some substring of $$$A$$$, and $$$D$$$ is some substring of $$$B$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If $$$X$$$ is a string, $$$|X|$$$ denotes its length."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A string $$$a$$$ is a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"substring"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of a string $$$b$$$ if $$$a$$$ can be obtained from $$$b$$$ by deletion of several (possibly, zero or all) characters from the beginning and several (possibly, zero or all) characters from the end."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A string $$$a$$$ is a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"subsequence"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of a string $$$b$$$ if $$$a$$$ can be obtained from $$$b$$$ by deletion of several (possibly, zero or all) characters. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Pay attention to the difference between the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"substring"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"subsequence"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", as they both appear in the problem statement. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You may wish to read the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longest_common_subsequence_problem"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Wikipedia page about the Longest Common Subsequence problem"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two positive integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n, m \\leq 5000$$$) — lengths of the two strings $$$A$$$ and $$$B$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a string consisting of $$$n$$$ lowercase Latin letters — string $$$A$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains a string consisting of $$$m$$$ lowercase Latin letters — string $$$B$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind"